{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120641","id":3936047383,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7qm1EX","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120641","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120641.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120641.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120641","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120641/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120641/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120641/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/9cc216073fb6bc7c6249f377c534461d5d563f3c","number":120641,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add modulate property to lightmaps.","user":{"login":"Skywolf285","id":49045791,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MDQ1Nzkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49045791?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Skywolf285","html_url":"https://github.com/Skywolf285","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Skywolf285/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Skywolf285/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Skywolf285/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Skywolf285/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Skywolf285/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Skywolf285/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Skywolf285/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Skywolf285/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Skywolf285/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nAdds a color property to lightmaps to multiple the final lightmap by. Effectively giving a limited way to alter the final lighting in real-time. Mostly useful to create day-night cycles but can have various other uses as well.\r\n\r\nI already wrote a more detailed reasoning in https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/14722\r\n\r\n- Closes #49968\r\n- Offers a potential solution for https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/11596\r\n\r\nEyecandy, using just LightmapGI and a few gradients to control the sky and lightmap color:\r\n<img width=\"570\" height=\"320\" alt=\"output\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/179d9737-3487-42bb-a527-08172e296d6a\" />\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nWill fully admit, I never touched C++ code so this entire thing is written using pattern observation, my best educated guess work and looking up basic C++ information whenever the syntax didn't make sense.\r\n\r\nFor the most part I'm pretty certain I did things the right way. The only thing I'm not certain about is how to update the lightmap captures. The problem I'm running into is that, to my knowledge, at no point a lightmap is aware what lightmap instances use it. Which is a problem because `LightStorage::Lightmap::modulate` has to be part of `LightStorage::Lightmap` to be accessible in the shader while `RendererSceneCull` needs a lightmap _instance_ to get the `RendererSceneCull::InstanceLightmapData` to call `RendererSceneCull::_instance_queue_update` on each of its geometries so the lightmap captures get properly updated.\r\n\r\nSo in order for lightmap captures to update whenever `LightStorage::lightmap_set_modulate` is called, did I store the lightmap instances for each lightmap in `LightStorage::Lightmap::lightmap_instances`. This feels like a very bad, hacky and error prone way to do things and requires each time a lightmap is assigned or removed to/from a lightmap instance `LightStorage::lightmap_insert_to_lightmap_instances` and/or `LightStorage::lightmap_erase_from_lightmap_instances` to be called.\r\n\r\nI considered other alternatives but each has their own drawbacks. Would love to have feedback on this. There is very non-zero chance I missed a better option here!\r\n\r\nAlso not sure about the UX. Because `LightStorage::Lightmap::modulate` is part of the lightmap does it appear under `Data/light_data` as part of the `LightmapGIData`  rather than under `Tweaks` where I feel it would be more logical. But to store the modulate property in both the LightmapGI node _and_ the `LightmapGIData` and carefully having to cover each scenario where these two might get out of sync doesn't sound great either. Not to mention it making it confusing where the modulate property is actually used.\r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-06-25T14:39:31Z","updated_at":"2026-07-08T12:42:05Z","closed_at":"2026-07-08T09:25:53Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"39cf454380ec3e120b87aff987ddf8660f73efa6","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"reques